# oracle: compute composition/atom cutoff 1.6 on a two-type fluid (fcc 0.8442, the atoms of one half of the box are type 2), 20 steps of nve; the neighbour count and the type fractions are dumped at step 20 and their sums are in thermo
# oracle: native: b332f28 (installed lmp; compute composition/atom is in the EXTRA-COMPUTE package of that binary)
# oracle-files: w227xc_composition.dump
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=none filerel=1e-12
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 2.3e-15, atoms n/a (atoms=none; the per-atom composition is the dump file, worst token 0).
units           lj
atom_style      atomic
lattice         fcc 0.8442
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            * 1.0
region          left block INF 3.0 INF INF INF INF units lattice
group           gleft region left
set             group gleft type 2
velocity        all create 1.2 87287 loop geom
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      * * 1.0 1.0 2.5
compute         comp all composition/atom cutoff 1.6
compute         compS all reduce sum c_comp[1] c_comp[2] c_comp[3]
dump            d1 all custom 20 w227xc_composition.dump id c_comp[1] c_comp[2] c_comp[3]
dump_modify     d1 sort id format float %.15g
fix             1 all nve
thermo_style    custom step pe ke c_compS[1] c_compS[2] c_compS[3]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             20
